1
00:00:00,664 --> 00:00:03,874
You video chat with Amy all the time.
How is this different?

2
00:00:04,042 --> 00:00:05,422
(Sheldon:)Don't you like Amy?

3
00:00:05,585 --> 00:00:08,295
- Of course, I like Amy.
- Well, there's the difference.

4
00:00:11,842 --> 00:00:13,672
(Leonard:)Excuse me, that's Priya.

5
00:00:14,177 --> 00:00:16,217
- Hi, Leonard.
- Hey, honey.

6
00:00:16,388 --> 00:00:18,678
- l miss you.
- Oh, I miss you too.

7
00:00:18,849 --> 00:00:20,019
(Sheldon:)I miss the old days...

8
00:00:20,183 --> 00:00:23,983
(Sheldon:)...when your romantic partners
could be returned to the video store.

9
00:00:26,648 --> 00:00:30,188
(Sheldon:)Thanks for letting me stay here while
Leonard Skypes with his girIfriend.

10
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,820
(Penny:)Oh, it's no problem.

11
00:00:31,987 --> 00:00:35,157
(Penny:)It's actually kind of nice.
You reading, me reading.

12
00:00:35,323 --> 00:00:37,613
(Penny:)We're like an old married couple.

13
00:00:38,451 --> 00:00:40,291
(Sheldon:)If we were an old married couple...

14
00:00:40,453 --> 00:00:43,913
(Sheldon:)...the wife would serve iced tea
and snickerdoodles.

15
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:47,627
(Penny:)I don't have iced tea
and snickerdoodles.

16
00:00:48,837 --> 00:00:51,837
(Sheldon:)A good wife would go to the store.

17
00:00:53,216 --> 00:00:55,466
(Penny:)I want a divorce.

18
00:00:55,635 --> 00:00:59,135
(Sheldon:)Good. On the way to see the lawyer,
pick up some tea and cookies.

19
00:01:04,477 --> 00:01:07,107
(Sheldon:)I must say,
I am enjoying your new chair.

20
00:01:07,272 --> 00:01:09,312
- Oh, it's great, isn't it?
- It is.

21
00:01:09,482 --> 00:01:14,192
(Sheldon:)Aligns the lumbar, cradles the coccyx,
balances the buttocks.

22
00:01:14,362 --> 00:01:17,492
(Sheldon:)- This is a chair worthy of the name.
- What name?

23
00:01:19,242 --> 00:01:20,782
(Sheldon:)Chair.

24
00:01:23,371 --> 00:01:24,751
(Penny:)Well, I'm glad you like it.

25
00:01:24,915 --> 00:01:28,415
(Penny:)I mean, I still can't get over the fact
someone just threw it away.

26
00:01:30,337 --> 00:01:32,337
- What?
- It was just sitting on the street.

27
00:01:32,505 --> 00:01:34,795
(Penny:)I paid a homeless guy
to help me get it up here.

28
00:01:34,966 --> 00:01:40,676
(Sheldon(jumps up):)Oh, dear. Oh, dear. Oh, dear.

29
00:01:41,306 --> 00:01:44,766
- What is wrong?
- I've been sitting in garbage.

30
00:01:45,268 --> 00:01:47,358
(Penny:)Sheldon, take it easy.

31
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:50,270
(Sheldon:)You take it easy.
I need to use your shower.

32
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:55,530
(Penny:)I went into this marriage
with so much hope.

33
00:01:57,197 --> 00:02:04,037
(Sheldon:)There's a wet Band-Aid
on the shower floor.

